  {
   "id": "I-002",
   "severity": "Informational",
   "evidence_level": "reasoning_only",
   "title": "Owner role is retained although it gates only the ownership transfer functions",
   "component": "StandardBEP20",
   "location": {
    "path": "StandardBEP20.sol",
    "start": 842,
    "end": 842
   },
   "category": "Other",
   "category_key": "evm.other",
   "description": [
    {
     "p": "StandardBEP20 inherits BEP20TokenOwner, which brings in the Ownable module and the getOwner view that the BEP20 interface expects. The onlyOwner modifier is applied only to renounceOwnership and transferOwnership. The token has a fixed supply minted once in the constructor, and the transfer, approve and transferFrom paths carry no owner hook, fee, pause or exclusion list. The owner therefore holds a title with the ability to pass it on or give it up, and nothing else."
    },
    {
     "p": "The current owner is the deployer account {{fact:onchain.owner}}, an externally owned account, which also received the whole initial supply. Holders are not exposed to owner action through the contract code; their exposure is limited to the deployer's token balance, which is a market consideration rather than a code one."
    }
   ],
   "impact": [
    {
     "p": "The role has no effect on balances, supply or transferability. Keeping it adds a privileged account that listing checkers and holders may read as a control surface that does not exist, and a lost owner key has no consequence beyond the getOwner value."
    }
   ],
   "recommendation": [
    {
     "ul": [
      "Document that the owner role exists only to satisfy the BEP20 getOwner convention and controls nothing in the token.",
      "If the role is meant to stay inert, consider renouncing it after listing requirements are met, or keep the key in cold storage."
     ]
    }
   ],
   "evidence": {
    "code": [
     {
