  {
   "id": "I-003",
   "severity": "Informational",
   "evidence_level": "reasoning_only",
   "title": "ServicePayer and IPayable are compiled into the source but unused by the deployed token",
   "component": "StandardBEP20",
   "location": {
    "path": "StandardBEP20.sol",
    "start": 767,
    "end": 779
   },
   "category": "Best practice",
   "category_key": "evm.best_practice",
   "description": [
    {
     "p": "The flattened source carries the IPayable interface and the abstract ServicePayer contract from the token-factory template. StandardBEP20 inherits ERC20Detailed and BEP20TokenOwner only, so ServicePayer is dead code in this file. The helper performs an external call with forwarded value in a constructor, which is the kind of code a reader of the verified source would expect to matter, and it adds review surface without behaviour."
    }
   ],
   "impact": [
    {
     "p": "There is no runtime effect. The unused contract lengthens the verified source and can mislead readers into assuming a deployment-fee payment that does not happen."
    }
   ],
   "recommendation": [
    {
     "ul": [
      "Remove IPayable and ServicePayer from the flattened source, or inherit ServicePayer if the fee payment is intended.",
      "Flatten only the inheritance chain that the final contract uses before verifying on the explorer."
     ]
    }
   ],
   "evidence": {
