  {
   "id": "I-004",
   "severity": "Informational",
   "evidence_level": "reasoning_only",
   "title": "Floating pragma leaves the compiler version open across every unit of the source",
   "component": "StandardBEP20",
   "location": {
    "path": "StandardBEP20.sol",
    "start": 836,
    "end": 842
   },
   "category": "Best practice",
   "category_key": "evm.best_practice",
   "description": [
    {
     "p": "Every unit in the file declares a caret pragma, so the source accepts any compiler release of the same series above the stated floor. The library units keep the caret because they are vendored, but the final StandardBEP20 unit should pin the exact version used for the verified build so that re-compilation reproduces the deployed bytecode and avoids picking up compiler changes that were not tested."
    }
   ],
   "impact": [
    {
     "p": "A re-deployment from the same source may compile with a different compiler than the one tested, which changes bytecode and can alter gas and edge behaviour. The deployed instance is unaffected."
    }
   ],
   "recommendation": [
    {
     "ul": [
      "Pin the pragma of the StandardBEP20 unit to the exact compiler version used for the verified deployment.",
      "Record the compiler version and optimizer settings alongside the source so the build can be reproduced."
     ]
    }
   ],
   "evidence": {
